.\specs\stories\sprint-status.yaml:992:  dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug: review                    # DEV COMPLETE 2026-08-14, awaiting code review, NOT committed. Delivered per all six ACs: isMeritEventGranted(rule) added to editor/merits.js (checks rule.special==='standing'), replacing the three broken rule.sub_category==='standing' checks (downtime-form.js:4210, merits.js buildMCIGrantOptions:410, buildFThiefOptions:463) and closing the fourth previously-unnamed defect (buildMeritOptions:314 gained the same check, alongside its own unrelated pre-existing sub_category filter, not replacing it). Confessor/Pledged now correctly appear at all three of AC2's replaced sites once their real Lance Status prereq is met - DISCOVERED DURING DEV, not assumed: buildMeritOptions does NOT make them selectable even after this fix, because that function's own pre-existing sub_category!=='general' check independently and correctly excludes anything tagged sub_category:'standing' (which Confessor/Pledged genuinely carry) - AC4's own wording was already scoped to AC2's three sites only, so this is not a defect, just a discovery the story's first test draft got wrong and corrected. TWO TEST-HARNESS BUGS (mine) found and fixed during dev: an afterAll teardown deleted a shared localStorage shim out from under a later describe block; a source-contract slice anchored on the wrong one of two literal "case 'merit':" occurrences in downtime-form.js. ONE REAL FALSE-PASS CAUGHT, not glossed over: isMeritEventGranted's own doc comment initially named buildMeritOptions and quoted meritPrereqOK(c, rule) close together in its prose, which satisfied n7-n9-allocator-readers.test.js's 600-char source-contract regex against the COMMENT TEXT rather than the real function - a green result for the wrong reason, caught by measuring actual character offsets rather than trusting the pass, reworded to fix. getItemsForCategory (downtime-form.js's own call site) is module-private with no exported setter and no lighter entry point than the full-DOM renderDowntimeTab, so proved via a source-contract test mirroring issue-896-availability-filter.test.js's own established pattern for this exact file, not direct invocation. 20 new tests in dbo-3-standing-merit-filter.test.js, full targeted gate with n7-n9-allocator-readers.test.js + issue-896-availability-filter.test.js = 68/69 - the 1 is the pre-existing, CLAUDE.md-documented #1115 failure, confirmed present on main BEFORE this story via git stash, not caused or worsened by DBO-3. Two prove-discrimination passes (neutralising isMeritEventGranted entirely; reverting only the new buildMeritOptions check), each a single-change revert, restored and re-verified green. Live tm_suite never connected to or written to during dev. No deploy, no migration, no commit to main - stays inside the pre-game freeze (game 2026-08-15). Full detail in dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug.md's Dev Agent Record. STORY CREATED 2026-08-14. Research pass (before writing ACs) found the epic's own naming (one call site, downtime-form.js) undersold the real scope: the SAME broken `rule.sub_category === 'standing'` check is duplicated at THREE sites across two files (downtime-form.js:4210, editor/merits.js:410 and :463), plus a FOURTH, previously-unnamed defect where merits.js:314's buildMeritOptions (the sheet's own primary Add Merit picker) has no standing-merit exclusion at all and lets MCI/PT slip through via a null-sub_category bypass. Live-data query against tm_suite (read-only, 2026-08-14) confirmed the epic's claim exactly: MCI and PT carry special:'standing'/sub_category:null; Confessor and Pledged (2 ordinary fixed-XP merits gated by a real Lance Status prereq the engine already evaluates, 0 characters currently own either) carry sub_category:'standing'/special:null - the wrong two merits have been excluded this whole time by coincidence, and the right two have never been excluded at all. Fix is a single shared exported predicate, isMeritEventGranted(rule) in editor/merits.js (checks rule.special==='standing'), replacing all three broken checks and added as a new check to buildMeritOptions - same shared-predicate-not-duplicated-logic pattern this session's own oxp-7 story (AC2, resolveHeldSeat) just established. Explicitly NOT a data write - Confessor/Pledged's live sub_category value is left as-is; the fix reads a different field, so the mislabeled value becomes irrelevant to this exclusion rather than needing correction, keeping the story inside the pre-game freeze (no tm_suite write of any kind). NOT DBO-1 - reads the same already-fetched rule documents, no schema change - but DBO-1 cross-referenced in Dev Notes: this story makes `special` load-bearing for the first time, raising DBO-1's stakes without resolving it. Four ACs map to the four call sites; AC6 requires real-shape test fixtures (matching the exact live special/sub_category/xp_fixed/prereq shapes) rather than simplified stand-ins, since the whole defect is a field-shape mismatch. Full detail and live-data findings in dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug.md's own Dev Notes. Branch: ms/dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug, cut fresh off main (oxp-7's own branch/commit kept separate per branch-hygiene call this session). Not deployed, not committed to main - per epic-dbo's own hard constraint, nothing from this repo deploys before the 2026-08-15 game.
